# sm109, the slow-dance farmer (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle sm109
revision 1
state ready
dialect southmeadow
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for tn_sm_iris_meadowfield
written_by claude
title the slow-dance farmer
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=farmer temper=calm
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk never_misses_a_harvest_dance
likes hard_cheese roof_birds festival_bells misty_dawns
dislikes wet_floors rats
fears knees_that_will_not_dance rats_in_the_seed_store
hopes the_young_ones_dancing_at_my_last_harvest a_dry_floor_and_a_full_loft
topics festival +0.4 work +0.3 family +0.3 animals +0.2 food +0.2 travel +0.2 gossip -0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=plain refuse=blunt tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# farms the home fields at an unhurried pace, says a thing straight and once, watches the swallows on the eaves, and has never sat out a harvest dance: the slow one at the end is always taken.

words
oath! = Rind and rafter | By the last slow turn
saying! = Say it once and say it straight | A slow foot still gets round the barn | Walk there once and you'll know the way home
dance = the dance at harvest end | the long slow dance at the end of harvest
lastturn = the last slow turn | the slow one at the end
cheese = a hard cheese | a wedge of hard cheese with a crust on it
swallows = the swallows under the eaves | the swallows on the ridge tiles
mist = a misty dawn | the mist lying on the low field
bells = the feast bells | the bells calling folk in for the dance
floor = a wet floor | muddy paws across my clean floor
ratword = the rats | those whiskered thieves in the loft
farm = the farm | the old farm
loft = the loft | the grain loft
young = the young ones | my pups
straight = and that's straight | plain as a gatepost
longwalk = the long walk north | the walk up north and home again

any
opinion @1 festivals for 3 : A harvest without #dance# is half a harvest. I'll be there while my legs will carry me, #straight#.
opinion @1 city against 1 : I walked to the city once. #good.capitalize# roads, poor air, and nobody knows the wolf next door. I came home.
opinion @1 houses for 1 : The Houses buy for the works, and the works buy our barley. I'll not grumble at a buyer, #straight#.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : Half of what a merchant asks is the merchant's own #supper#. I'd rather sell at the gate myself.
opinion @1 times for 1 : A full loaf and a dry roof. I'm not one to want for more, #straight#.
opinion @1 watch against 1 [self.robbed=yes] : They never found who robbed me, and they didn't look long. #bad.capitalize# work, that.
opinion @2 watch mixed 0 : The watch keep the toll and the gate. Past that, I couldn't tell you what they're for, #address#.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Say what you want and I'll say if I can help. | #greet#. You've come a way, by the dust on you.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=farmer] : #greet#. Talk while I work; #farm# won't wait. | #greet#. Mind where you tread, the sowing's in.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn here.weather=fog] : #greet#. #mist.capitalize#. Best start a day can have. | #greet#. You came out of the mist like a ghost.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Late, but the door's not shut yet. | #greet#. Supper's done, so you'll have to sit hungry.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are. Wipe your feet before #floor# sees you. | Oh, it's you. Come in, and mind #floor#.
line @1 again.open : Back already. I've not budged, #straight#. | You twice in a day. Somebody's after something, #straight#.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. I'm well. Ask me no more than that.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Sit yourself down. | #greet#. I'd the kettle on for somebody.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Busy, but not so busy as to be rude. | #greet#. I'll talk and work both.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Late for calling, but come in. | #greet#. It's dark, so be quick.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the ditch by the gate.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #s8_night#. | #farewell#. Watch the lane in the dark.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #s8_byeback#.
line @1 react.news : #ack#. Well, there it is. | #surprise#. You don't say. Go on.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. Not a word of that had reached me. | #marvel#. First I've heard.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. Old as last week's #cheese#. | I had that already. Fair of you to tell me, though.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. I'll hear it from a second mouth first. | That's not the way I heard it, #straight#.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. I'm sorry for it. | That's a #bad# thing. No use pretending it isn't.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. That'll want a dance. | #good.capitalize# news. I'm glad of it.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. | Well enough. Nothing to #grumble# about. | #good.capitalize#. Slow, but good.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. It'll be done when it's done. | Plenty to do. I'll do it at my pace, #slow# or not.
line @1 ask.how : And you? Out with it, straight. | How are you keeping, #address#?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit; it'll keep while you do. | That's #bad#. I'm sorry for it, and I'll not dress it up.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, but no. I've the day's #work# to see to, and it won't see to itself. | I'd not manage it. My pace is #slow# and the day's full.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. | Fair. Another day will do, #address#.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. | That's a kindness. I'll not let it slip my mind.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. | Nothing to it. You'd have done the same, #address#.
line @1 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | That's me said my piece.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. #s8_okay#. | Off with you. #work.capitalize# will keep me.
line @1 ack : #ack#. | #bc_right#
rule @rats
when concept=bark working=yes self.dislikes=rats
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Out of #loft#, you thieves. Out. | There's droppings in the seed again. #annoyed#.

rule @wetfloor
when concept=bark here.weather=rain self.dislikes=wet_floors
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wipe your feet, whoever you are. #annoyed#. | #floor.capitalize#. #grumble#.

rule @feastday
when concept=bark here.day=festival
does aside
cooldown 12h
say #bells.capitalize#. Where's that blue shawl got to. | There's #dance# tonight, and I'll be at it.

rule @eaves
when concept=bark working=no here.time=dusk self.likes=roof_birds
does aside
cooldown 12h
say There go #swallows#. Home for the night, same as me. | Look at them stitch the sky. #tasty.capitalize#, that.

scene misty_morning
when topic=weather|day here.weather=fog here.time=dawn
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess / ack
a : #mist.capitalize#. Give me that over a clear sky any day. | Can't see the far hedge this morning. #very.capitalize# fine, I call it. | The mist's down on the low field. Sound carries strange in it.
b : It's damp, mind. | Hard to see your way. | Strange how?
a : Damp's no matter, so long as it stays off #floor#. | I know my way blind. The lane hasn't moved since I was a #child#. | A cart two fields off sounds like it's at the gate. You get used to it, #address#.
b? : #bc_fair_enough# | Ha. | #bc_i_know#

scene dance_years
when topic=festival|memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I count my years in dances, not birthdays. It's kinder that way. | There's #dance# soon. I've not sat one out yet, and I'll not start. | I take #lastturn# with whoever asks. That's my rule.
b : How many dances, then? | Not even one? | Whoever?
a : Enough that I've stopped counting the birthdays, #straight#. | Not one. I'd crawl to #dance# before I'd miss it. | Whoever. I tell them if they tread on me, mind.

scene slow_steps
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The young ones want reels. Give me #lastturn#, where you can hear yourself think. | I'm no quick dancer. I'm a steady one, #straight#. | A dance isn't a race. Folk forget that after the third cup of #ale#.
b : The reels are fun, though. | What's the difference? | They do forget.
a : For them. I'll watch and keep the beat with my foot. | Quick ones fall over. Steady ones finish. #saying.capitalize#. | And then they fall over. #bc_every_year#

scene bells_on_feast
when topic=festival|season self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #bells.capitalize#. I hear them from my door and start looking for my shawl. | There's no sound I like better than #bells# on a feast morning. | The bells ring and I put the work down. Nobody argues with me.
b : Which shawl? | Not one? | Nobody?
a : The blue one. It's seen more of #dance# than most wolves. | Not one. Not even #swallows#. | Nobody that's tried twice, #straight#.

scene cheese_crust
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #cheese.capitalize#, an onion and a heel of bread. That's dinner, and a #good# one. | I'll not eat soft cheese. It's not finished, is how I see it. | Keep the crust on. That's where the #tasty# part is, whatever anyone says.
b : Simple and good. | Not finished? | Some folk cut it off.
a : Simple's what I like. Fuss is for #toffs#. | It hasn't sat long enough to have anything to say. | Some folk are wrong. I tell them so, #straight#.

scene eaves_swallows
when topic=animals|smalltalk self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I sit on the step of an evening and watch #swallows#. Better than any talk. | #swallows.capitalize# came back this year. Same nest, I'd say. | There's a starling on my roof that does the cockerel. Fools the hens every time.
b : What's to watch? | The same birds? | Every time?
a : How they turn. Not a feather out of place. They'd dance well. | The same mess on the step, so I'd think so. | Every time. The hens never learn, and nor does the starling.

scene loft_rats
when topic=animals|work self.dislikes=rats
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #ratword.capitalize# have been at the seed again. I'll have them out if I have to sleep up there. | I found a nest of them in the sacks. #annoyed#, I said, and worse. | A rat in the loft eats a row of barley by spring. I've done the sums.
b : Get a cat. | I don't blame you. | That's a lot of barley.
a : I've two. They're frightened of #ratword#. | Don't. I blame myself for not looking sooner. | It is. And I'll not feed rats on my own seed, #straight#.

scene wet_floor
when topic=home here.weather=rain
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #rain.capitalize#, and every paw in the house walks it across my floor. | I scrubbed that floor at dawn. Look at it. #floor.capitalize#. | A wet floor's worse than a wet field. You can't plough a kitchen.
b : It's only water. | It'll dry. | Ha. That's true.
a : Water and mud and whatever's in the yard. It's never only water. | It'll dry when they stop walking on it, and they won't. #bc_never# | It's true, and nobody's laughing in my kitchen, #straight#.

scene the_farm
when topic=work|land self.job=farmer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've farmed these fields since before my teeth were set. I know every stone in them. | Barley on the top, wheat in the middle, and the low field for whatever'll take the wet, #address#. | I don't hurry #farm#. It doesn't hurry for me.
b : Every stone? | Why the low field? | Is that a good way?
a : Every one. I've tripped on most of them, #straight#. | The mist sits there. Barley sulks in it; beans don't mind. | It's the only way. Hurry, and you sow twice. #saying.capitalize#.

scene harvest_end
when topic=harvest|work here.season=autumn self.job=farmer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The last load's in #loft#, and the dance is Restday. I'll sleep till then. | Harvest done. I'm #tired# and bent like a nail, and I don't care. | We got it in before the rain. That's the only harvest that matters.
b : You've earned it. | Bent nail? | Good timing.
a : I've earned #lastturn#, and I'll take it. | Bent, but it'll straighten for #dance#. Always does. | Timing and luck, half and half. I'll take either.

scene young_ones
when topic=family self.parent=yes self.job=farmer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #young.capitalize# think I'm slow. I'm not slow. I'm early and patient. | Whatever else they learn, #self.child# will learn to dance. That's my one rule. | I'd give #young# the farm tomorrow, if the farm were ready for them.
b : Is there a difference? | Only the one rule? | Aren't they ready?
a : Ask them who gets #work# done first. | Only the one I'll fight for. The rest they can argue, #straight#. | They're ready. #farm.capitalize# is the stubborn one.

scene straight_talk
when topic=smalltalk|friends
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Ask me a thing and I'll answer it straight. Folk don't always thank me for it. | I don't sweeten things. You get what I think, once, and then we move on. | My #mum# said I'd tell the Bright One the sermon was too long.
b : That's honest. | Once? | Would you?
a : It's cheaper than lying. You don't have to remember it. | Once. Saying it twice is nagging, and I'll not nag, #address#. | I'd tell it kindly. But I'd tell it, #straight#.

scene times_steady
when topic=times|prices world.times=ordinary|good|boom self.job=farmer
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : There's bread on my table. I'll not grumble at the times. | The grain sells and the roof holds. That's a #good# year, by me. | Folk always want more. I've enough, and I know it, #straight#.
b : Not everyone's so lucky. | What more is there? | That's rare.
a : No. I know that too, and I'm thankful. | A dry floor, maybe. I'll settle for the roof. | Rare, but it's not hard. You stop counting. #saying.capitalize#.

scene times_lean
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean self.job=farmer
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : Lean times. We'll eat #cheese# and keep the soft for selling. | It's a thin year. #farm.capitalize# has had thin years before and kept going. | Prices are down at the gate. I'll hold the grain a while yet.
b : Will it pass? | You've seen worse? | Is that wise?
a : It always has. Slow, but it does. #reassure#. | Worse and longer. We danced through those too. #bc_i_know# | Wise or stubborn. Ask me in spring, #straight#.

scene robbed_once
when topic=crime self.robbed=yes
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : I was robbed, and the watch never found who. I've stopped expecting it. | They took from me and walked off, and nobody's answered for it. | Since I was robbed I bar the loft at night. I never used to.
b : That's not right. | That's hard. | Wise.
a : It's not. But it's done, and I'll not chew it forever. | Hard, and over. I'll leave it there, #straight#. | Wise, or sad. A bit of both.

scene faith_plain
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Me and the Bright One have a bargain. I work, it rains, mostly. | I go to chapel at festival and give at #work#. That's my share. | I pray for dry floors and wet fields. One out of two'd do.
b : Mostly? | That's fair. | Which one?
a : Mostly. I'll not complain of the rest. | Fair is all I aim at. #bc_fair# | The fields. #floor.capitalize# I can mop myself.

scene gossip_plain
when topic=gossip
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's all I heard, and I'll not stretch it. | They're saying #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Make of it what you like. | Folk are full of it: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'll wait and see.
b : That's news. | What's your guess? | Wise to wait.
a : News, aye. Gossip, mostly. I'll know which by spring. | No guessing till I know more, #straight#. | Waiting costs nothing. Being wrong costs #money#.

scene stiff_knees
when topic=health self.age>=45
does tell.self / sympathise / assess
a : My knees creak on the stair, but they'll still do #lastturn#. | I've an ache in the hip that comes with the rain. It's a better almanac than any. | I'm slower than I was. I was never fast, so it's not much of a loss.
b : Look after them. | A good almanac, that. | Slow's no bad thing.
a : I will. They've a dance to get to. | Right more often than the chapel, #straight#. | No. #slow.capitalize#'s how I got here.

story long_walk [topic=travel|memories self.away=no self.age>=30]
  : I walked to the city once. All the way. Took me most of a week.
  : I saw the towers and the river and the crowds, and I bought a ribbon I've never worn.
  : Then I set my face south and came home. Best part of the trip, #longwalk#.
  ask : Have you ever been, yourself?
  b[from=ridgemere] : Born there. I'd not walk it, though.
  b : Not yet. You'd not go back, then?
  : Once was enough. I know the way home now, #straight#.

story first_dance [topic=festival|memories self.age>=25]
  : The first harvest dance I went to, I was a #child# and nobody would take my paw.
  : So I danced with a sheaf. Round and round the barn, on my own.
  : An old farmer cut in, bowed to the sheaf, and took me for #lastturn#.
  b : That's a kind one. Who was it?
  : I never found out. I've taken a little one for the last dance every harvest since.

story flooded_barn [topic=festival|lore self.age>=30]
  : One harvest the storm came down the night of the dance and flooded the barn ankle-deep.
  : Nobody went home. We took our shoes off and danced in it till the fiddler's candle went out.
  ask : Would you have stayed, or gone home dry?
  b : I'd have stayed. You only get one dance a harvest.
  b[old] : I remember that night. I lost a shoe in it.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Say what you need, plain, and I'll say if I can. | #greet#. I've a minute. Make it count.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Back again. Sit if you like. | #topic.player#. #greet#. What is it this time?
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=farmer] : I'm the one who #self.trade_words#. Barley, wheat, beans, and rats when I'm unlucky. | Sowing, weeding, cutting, carting. #farm.capitalize# takes the year, and I let it.
dlg @2 resident.job : #job_busy# | This and that, and none of it fast, #address#.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# | Nothing's come my way worth repeating, #straight#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I don't trade in that. Ask a #busybody# with more time.
dlg @1 resident.business [business!=thriving|failing] : Steady. The grain sells, slow and sure, #straight#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the ditch by the gate.
graft resident.hub
choice Is it true you've never missed a harvest dance? -> dances
node dances
say True. Not one. I've danced with a sprained tail and a heavy cold. I'll take #lastturn# with anybody who asks, and tell them if they tread on me.
mood pleased
free
choice Why the last dance? -> lastdance
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node lastdance
say It's slow, so you can talk, and it's last, so nobody's in a hurry. An old farmer once took me for it when I was small. I pay it back.
choice That's kind. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
